<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n14080" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Dīphĭlus</span></b> , i,
			m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Δίφιλος</span>. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A celebrated Greek comic writer of Sinope, imitated
				by Plautus</i>, <i><span class="en">Plaut. Cas. prol. 32</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. Rud.
				prol. 32</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Ter. Ad. prol. 6</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Vell. 1,
				16, 3</span></i>. —</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>An architect employed by Quintus Cicero</i>, <i><span class="en">Cic. Q. Fr.
				3, 1, 1</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>III.</b>
			<i>Secretary of Crassus</i>, <i><span class="en">Cic. de
				Or. 1, 30, 136</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
